# What must NOT be sent into the build context.
#
# Docker looks for the ignore file next to the Dockerfile first, under the name
# "<dockerfile name>.dockerignore", and only then in the context root as
# ".dockerignore". That is how every example in this course gets its own rules
# while they all share a single context.

# Build output produced on the host. It does not belong in the image - the
# image builds everything itself. It is also compiled for Windows, whereas
# the container runs on Linux.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# History and tooling settings.
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/
.editorconfig

# Course material. Docker reads the Dockerfile itself separately,
# so there is no need to ship it inside the context.
case-study-a-dockerfile/
case-study-b-tooling/
case-study-c-configuration/
*.md
